# Canonical authorship for this repository.
#
# The correct identity is:
#     muneebexotic <muneebusman112233@gmail.com>
#
# Early commits — including the whole of the pushed
# milestone-0-security-remediation branch — were made under a machine-global
# git identity that belongs to different accounts:
#
#     muneebexotic3 <musman@innovative-pk.com>
#
# Those commits are already on the remote, and rewriting them would need a
# force push, which is out of scope here. A mailmap fixes the attribution
# **without touching history**: `git log`, `git blame`, and `git shortlog`
# all honour it, and it costs nothing to carry.
#
# Two things it does NOT do:
#   1. GitHub links a commit to an account by the raw author email, so the
#      web UI will still show those commits as unattributed until history is
#      rewritten.
#   2. It does not stop a wrong identity being used again — the pre-commit
#      hook does that.
#
# To make it permanent, the history purge in SECURITY-REMEDIATION.md §2.5
# should pass `--mailmap ../.mailmap` to git-filter-repo. That rewrite is
# already planned, so the correction is free if it happens then.
#
# Format: <canonical name> <canonical email> <wrong name> <wrong email>

